#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:5
#: 865897cda8d74b869818d10265e765ff
msgid "Indoor Flying Guidelines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:7
#: 53c0786140c24f32823237064848b434
msgid "This article provides guidelines for flying your multicopter inside without any position or velocity source (e.g. no GPS, no optical flow). For indoor flight using a non-GPS position or velocity source please refer to the :ref:`Non-GPS Navigation <common-non-gps-navigation-landing-page>` page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:12
#: c62abb7ba9174abe8ab6a8c23626b348
msgid "When flying indoors make sure you have plenty of space and follow safety procedures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:14
#: 313d099b2ef044bfa75e180ac1bc304d
msgid "GPS does not work indoors and needs to be disabled (no exceptions)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:17
#: 0d137fd27a2540a7a80b83601301fe13
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:19
#: ea925d12d9c74cce9ed50439443ab2ab
msgid "The main point note when flying indoors is that Global Positioning Systems will not work. Even if you see that you have the correct number of satellites and a low HDOP, this is due to multipathing of the signals from the satellites. This means the single is being reflected to the antenna via walls, windows and other surfaces from outside. If you look at the position on a map you will see that the location will not match your current location, or will be drifting, at time many meters or even 1000s of metres from your location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:29
#: aa133efeb4ce41f9944d5746c3b018a0
msgid "Stabilize"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:31
#: 685f3fbec96c4ce6aea1a38744e788b9
msgid ":ref:`Stabilize <stabilize-mode>` mode does not use GPS, and has the least problems, but the pilot will need good control of the copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:35
#: 6b37a82458ef463e92521bbbf270dca1
msgid "Altitude Hold"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:37
#: a7337a41bf0e463593c2aba16e0dc3da
msgid ":ref:`Altitude Hold <altholdmode>` mode use the barometer to hold a specific altitude. The barometer relies on a constant air pressure. Air-pressure in a room can change due to doors opening or closing. Also climate control devices like fans and air-conditioning will also cause pressure changes. The likely outcome is a sudden crash in the floor or ceiling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:45
#: 72785ce9611f4647a0393d74c9fe935c
msgid "Sonar or Lidar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:47
#: 51fd6cbe93ab408383905b22b8a190ca
msgid "Using a downward facing :ref:`sonar or lidar <common-rangefinder-landingpage>` when flying in :ref:`AltHold <altholdmode>` can help avoid sudden changes in altitude causing crashes into the floor or ceiling.  See :ref:`Surface Tracking <terrain-following-manual-modes>` for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:50
#: e9c497c4a8f642cab08179ec177a890e
msgid "Safe Indoor Flying Dos"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:52
#: 70c0598a2f914737bdcaee996866fbc4
msgid "Disable the GPS by setting :ref:`GPS1_TYPE<GPS1_TYPE>` to 0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:53
#: 9cfc23301fc74f528c3fe5aa8b04e410
msgid "Configure the :ref:`battery failsafe <failsafe-battery>` to \"Land\" by setting :ref:`BATT_FS_LOW_ACT <BATT_FS_LOW_ACT>` = 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:54
#: f10fdb7700ff490295d5e3c83eeb3a92
msgid "Configure the :ref:`radio failsafe <radio-failsafe>` to \"Enabled always Land\" by setting :ref:`FS_THR_ENABLE <FS_THR_ENABLE>` = 3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:55
#: 2151906db6d9463690970a131e28a99d
msgid "Disable the :ref:`fence <common-geofencing-landing-page>` by setting :ref:`FENCE_ENABLE <FENCE_ENABLE>` = 0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:56
#: bfceb39e2aa34066b33d8bd4faca8450
msgid "Use a downward facing sonar or lidar (if available)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:59
#: 406c736208a742899dd0379955ce8e38
msgid "Safe Indoor Flying Don'ts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:61
#: 82699eaf001a4c748745d5984387c297
msgid "Don't fly in small confined spaces. Use common sense, flying inside a warehouse with a high roof = OK, bedroom = not OK."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:63
#: 95ed2d4c465c4177ae2d1a2749330bbd
msgid "Don't use Auto\\* modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:65
#: 7d95772b146b4a5291fec5f3d33a9c58
msgid "\\* Autonomous and semi-autonomous modes require a position estimate. This can come from GPS or from :ref:`Non-GPS Navigation <common-non-gps-navigation-landing-page>` sources such as optical flow, external navigation, or motion capture systems. In ArduPilot 4.7 and later, the EKF origin can be automatically saved and restored across power cycles — see :ref:`Persistent Origin Storage <common-non-gps-navigation-landing-page>` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:67
#: 64a8a1dc83ec4ad2a54fb58cce3a4dd0
msgid "\\*\\* Non-autonomous modes include :ref:`Stabilize <stabilize-mode>` and :ref:`AltHold <altholdmode>`"
msgstr ""
